WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:04.037
 Jay, Stephan, congratulations.

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.072
You're both in the final round.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.074
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges,

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.542
where you're nice
and comfortable,

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.012
to make an iconic
weapon from history--

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:17.984
the Zweihander.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.318
[music playing]

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.254
The Zweihander, which
means two-hander in German,

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.223
was a massive sword wielded
by Swiss and German mercenary

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.158
armies in the 16th century.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.627
Sometimes stretching to
over six feet in length,

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:32.332
the Zweihander was a long sword
featuring an extended grip

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:33.499
and broad guard.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:36.268
As European armies employed
more pikes and polearms

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:38.170
on the battlefield,
the Zweihander

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:39.972
emerged as a counter weapon.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.708
This enormous sword
was used to break up

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.577
pike formations by cutting
spear-ends and opening

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.845
up holes in enemy lines.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:49.248
Due to its size, the Zweihander
was only wielded by the biggest

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.784
and most audacious soldiers.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.686
If these soldiers survived
charges into enemy spears,

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:56.823
they would often be paid double
for their substantial risk.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.492
The Zweihander eventually
faded from the battlefield,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:03.396
but survives today in
games such as "Dark Souls."

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:07.333
It must be an effective
working version of that weapon.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.469
JAY: I've never made
a Zweihander before.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.371 line:0%
Of course, I've never made
a friction folder either,

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.139 line:7%
but that turned out OK, right?

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.775 line:7%
[laughs nervously]

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:20.046
HOST: Your blade must have a
double edged flamberged blade,

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:24.350
guard, ricasso,
pommel, and two lugs.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:25.752
You will have five
days at your home

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.419
forge to complete
this challenge.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.022
At the end of those
five days, you

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.390
will return and
present your weapons

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.425
to our panel of expert judges.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.926
Only after they've
submitted them

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.130
to a series of brutal tests
will they declare one of you

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:38.197
the champion.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.432
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.802
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.536 line:0%
STEPHAN: Today, we're
going to forge the Damascus

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.573 line:0%
and get our rough
forged blank, hopefully.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.176 line:0%
I'm looking for
about 200, maybe 250

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:52.645 line:7%
layer ladder pattern Damascus.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.080
One thing I like to do when I
really want to just kind of get

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:57.016
into it and [growling]
rock it out,

00:01:57.082 --> 00:01:59.419
I'll eat a super spicy pepper.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.354
[grunt] Yeah!

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.222 line:7%
Let's go!

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.959 line:0%
JAY: So far, it's coming
together really good.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:10.663
My grind marks meet up right
here in the center really good.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.266
It's time to quench.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:16.369
When you have a
five-foot blade, that

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.705
means you had to have almost
a five-foot quench tank, which

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.241
means now to get the
blade in the quench tank,

00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:25.177
you're at 10 feet in the air.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:26.946
This can be pretty bad.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:28.848
If the quench doesn't
go good, we're

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.216
gonna have to start all over.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:37.924 line:7%
Sweet.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.492 line:7%
It didn't break.

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:42.161
That's what I was hoping for.

00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:44.397
Now I can start
working on the guard.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.334
 The scallops look good.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:52.104
I got the handle glued
on and tightened down.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.908
So today we're gonna get
it sharp and test it.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.713
I'll see your watermelon
and raise you a bucket.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.120
[music playing]

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.554
 This blade is a beast.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.823
It's gonna be able
take some punishment

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.858
and deal some punishment.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:21.701
[chuckles] It will cut.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.604
 Now, the Zweihander was known
as a weapon of intimidation.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.906
To test the sharpness
of your edge,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:30.309
I'm going to cut into this
bundle of sugar cane twice--

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.412
once with either side.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.612
Jay, you're up first.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:34.413
Are you ready?

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:36.048
 Ready as I'm ever gonna be.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.650 line:7%
I know my blade's sharp.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:38.584 line:7%
I know it'll do good.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.386
I'm expecting
something epic, but

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:43.289
until it's really put to the
test, you just never know.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.871
[music playing]

00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:03.276
 It's got a lot
of weight to it,

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:06.913
but obviously it's plenty sharp.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:07.980
Nicely done.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.048
 Thank you.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:09.915
DAVE: All right,
Stephan, you're up.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:10.649
Are you ready?

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:11.584
 Can't wait.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.085 line:0%
Jay's weapon did
really well cutting

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.320 line:7%
through the sugar canes.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:15.921
I'm not nervous about
mine, but, you know,

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.857
I don't know if it's
gonna cut better than his.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:18.791
His cut real strong.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:32.405
 It's light.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.107
It's easy to wield.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:37.976
That guard-- it's almost
where it's into you

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:39.946
when you're swinging it.

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:42.014
You can see it cut
deep and clean.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:45.351
It looks like the blade held
up beautifully, so nice job.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:46.352
 Thank you.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:52.725
 Bladesmiths, the Zweihander
was a weapon of war.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.493
Big weapon, big damage.

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:56.395
I will take your weapon
and deliver killing

00:04:56.461 --> 00:04:57.963
blows on this ballistic dummy.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.933
Let's see how much damage
your weapon can do.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:01.767
Jay, you're up first.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:02.334
You ready?

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:03.169
 Go for it.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:03.970
MAN: Let's do this.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:11.911
[music playing]

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:22.955
It is a heavy weight, and
it's harder to manipulate

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.190
with multiple blows.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:30.129
But on the thrust, I was able to
go in one side and all the way

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.431
on the opposite
side of the dummy.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.000
This, sir, will kill.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:35.968
 Thank you.

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.570
 Stephan, you're up next.

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:38.137
You ready?

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:38.971
 Absolutely.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.140
MAN: Let's do this.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:44.344
[music playing]

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.026
 That was brutal.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:03.162
 OK, Steve, the
edge of your sword

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:06.799
is sharp enough to lacerate
all the way into the ribs,

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:11.437
and on the power strike, that
would disembowel and ruin

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.438
this person.

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:14.040
 That's the idea.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.875
 This sword will kill.

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:17.643
Good job.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.444
 Thank you.

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:22.047
DAVE: Gentlemen, this
is the strength test.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:25.384
Now, the Zweihander was often
used against pike formations,

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.286
so I'm gonna take
yours Zweihanders

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.089
and go against a rack
of pikes here five times

00:06:30.155 --> 00:06:34.093
with each of your blades, see
how far I can break through.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:34.927
Jay, you're up.

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:35.761
Are you ready?

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:36.529
 Ready.

00:06:39.998 --> 00:06:42.935
[music playing]

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:54.379
 Wow.

00:06:54.446 --> 00:06:55.982
When you start
swinging this thing,

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.350
it moves things out of its way.

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:01.820
I don't see any
damage to your edge.

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:02.955
Nicely done.

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:04.123
 Thank you.

00:07:04.189 --> 00:07:05.857
 All right, Steve, you're up.

00:07:05.924 --> 00:07:06.392
 Do it.

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:07.626
DAVE: OK.

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:09.128
 The third test
is probably the one

00:07:09.194 --> 00:07:10.563 line:7%
I'm the most confident about.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.464 line:0%
You know, I've-- I've beat
the heck out of this sword,

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:13.766 line:7%
and it's doing well.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.836
So now it's just how much
mayhem can Dave cause.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:23.109
[music playing]

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.887
Obviously, it's a good cutter.

00:07:35.954 --> 00:07:37.589
It actually bit into
that wood and split

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:39.858
that right down the middle.

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:43.396
Very easy to wield because
of its light weight,

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:47.533
but I think we've bent
just a little bit.

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:51.971
It's bent in two directions,
and there is a crack now

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:55.340
developing in the handle.

00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:57.243
 Gentlemen, we've
got a lot to discuss.

00:07:57.309 --> 00:07:59.145
We'll see you back at the forge.

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:00.413
 I'm concerned.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.448
I had a warp in my blade,
so I don't know who's

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.883
gonna end up with the win.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:10.089
 Bladesmiths, the judges have
made their final decision.

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:12.992
It's time to declare one of you
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:17.596 --> 00:08:21.099
Jay, congratulations.

00:08:21.166 --> 00:08:25.471
Stephan, unfortunately your
sword did not make the cut.

00:08:25.537 --> 00:08:26.939
Dave will explain.

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:28.874
 Stephan, I think what
you did with your steel is

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:32.678
visually stunning, but
what this came down to

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:33.980
was the strength test.

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:37.449 line:0%
When your handle developed
a bend in two directions,

00:08:37.482 --> 00:08:40.453 line:0%
that caused a stress
fracture in the handle,

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.121 line:0%
as well as a slight bend
right where the lugs are.

00:08:43.188 --> 00:08:46.926
And it's those reasons combined
that are sending you home.

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:47.860
 I understand.

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:51.430
 Stephan, please
surrender your weapon.

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:52.698
STEPHAN: I'm disappointed.

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:55.634
I really wanted to
win, but that's OK.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.269
I love being at the forge.

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:58.036
It's hot.

00:08:58.103 --> 00:08:59.004
It's dirty.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:03.208
You'll smell funny,
but it is so rewarding.

00:09:03.275 --> 00:09:04.410
HOST: Jay, congratulations.

00:09:04.477 --> 00:09:05.911
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:06.512
Good job.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:08.046
[applause]

00:09:08.113 --> 00:09:09.648
 Thank you.

00:09:09.714 --> 00:09:11.083
HOST: How do you feel right now?

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.886
 I feel like my heart's about
to burst out of my chest.

00:09:13.952 --> 00:09:16.355
 Well, it's the heaviest
weapon I've ever had

00:09:16.421 --> 00:09:17.890
to wield in this competition.

00:09:17.957 --> 00:09:21.059
Very well balanced and
a powerful weapon, too.

00:09:21.126 --> 00:09:21.927
 Thank you.

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:23.395
 And the way you
built your handle--

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:26.666 line:0%
that tells me a lot about
the way that you make things.

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:29.368 line:0%
The wood is fitted on and
then wrapped with leather

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:31.704 line:0%
with these reinforcing
pieces underneath.

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:34.372 line:0%
That's the proper
way to construct it.

00:09:34.439 --> 00:09:35.774
 Thank you.

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:39.044
 Well, Jay, in exchange for
that sword and those socks--

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:40.045
[chuckling]

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:42.948
--you will be receiving
that check for $10,000.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.250
JAY: When they announced
that I was the winner,

00:09:45.317 --> 00:09:46.485
it felt really good.

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:47.753
I've had people
tell me, you know,

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.388
you're good at what
you do, but I always

00:09:49.454 --> 00:09:51.056
have this kind of self-doubt.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.126
To make it all the way to
the end and be the champion,

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.995
I'm so happy.

